		{
			"id": "112100546021712622",
			"parentId": "112100214465796095",
			"url": "https://social.anoxinon.de/@thurti/112100545960592639",
			"author": {
				"name": "thurti",
				"url": "https://social.anoxinon.de/@thurti",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/314/593/032/380/929/original/8a60fd575ce8ed01.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-03-15T16:03:04.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Sorry for being passive aggressive myself, I didn't mean to get personal. We should definitely criticize code. And there is a lot to criticize in this example. </p><p>I just got the feeling from reading the comments that all the tailwind and js bashing is becoming a cult itself.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112100643652950151",
			"parentId": "112100546021712622",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/112100643652950151",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-03-15T16:27:55.271Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://social.anoxinon.de/@thurti\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>thurti</span></a></span> no worries!</p><p>Yeah, I can see that criticism too. I have thought about it a lot. It’s easy to dismiss the criticism as a Nickleback style level-of-popularity pushback, but I think it goes deeper.</p><p>I think Tailwind in particular receives a lot of deserved criticism because they go pretty headstrong in their marketing almost to the point of being anti-CSS—specifically the line “best practices don’t work” that’s been on their home page for many years.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112101191098844814",
			"parentId": "112100643652950151",
			"url": "https://social.anoxinon.de/@thurti/112101191003295906",
			"author": {
				"name": "thurti",
				"url": "https://social.anoxinon.de/@thurti",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/314/593/032/380/929/original/8a60fd575ce8ed01.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-03-15T18:47:07.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Yeah, they have some bold statements on their website. </p><p>The more I think about it, I feel like the whole thing is just a clever business model.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
